Before everybody rushes off to debate this, anybody want to try it?
Sunday night I wrote up the code to do this; the diff to end.c is
included below.

Please note: this is not an "official patch," I am not on the dev
team, and neither they nor I have any intention of supporting this
through future upgrades.  This is merely intended for people who
like hacking the code (this is Hack, after all), so that if this
idea is discussed, people actually have some hard idea of the end
result.  Perhaps if people are interested, we could polish the
idea a little before submitting it.

Again, in the words of The Dev Team (from the README):

	If you decide to apply a free-lanced patch to your 3.0
	code, you are on your own.  In our own patches, including
	those which will update to 3.1, we will assume that your
	code is synchronized with ours.

Also, I suspect neither I nor any of the usual archive sites will
keep this.

Now that I've scared most people off, here is the diff.  Apply it
to a fresh 3.0j "end.c."  Oh, yes, you will probably want to keep the
original end.c around.  Cheers!

